For more than two decades, Bishop Fox has defined the forefront of offensive security. By combining elite human expertise with the power of its proprietary Cosmos AI engine, the firm delivers industry-leading cloud and application security services, including AI-powered penetration testing and AI/LLM security assessments that reflect real-world attacker behavior. Renowned for its innovation and contributions to the open-source community through flagship tools like &nbsp;Sliver &nbsp;and AIMap , Bishop Fox has released 25+ tools and 75+ advisories in the last 10 years.&nbsp;

As a trusted partner to the world’s most recognizable brands, Bishop Fox protects 26 of the Fortune 100, eight of the top 10 global tech companies, all of the top five global media companies, 10 of the top 20 retailers and seven 7 of the top 10 manufacturers. A consistent market leader, Bishop Fox has been recognized as a Leader and "Fast Mover" in the GigaOm Radar for Attack Surface Management for five consecutive years. With a 70 NPS rating, the firm remains the trusted partner for organizations seeking to stay ahead of the evolving threat landscape. Learn more at bishopfox.com

Who You Are and What You'll Do&nbsp;

We are seeking a highly organized, emotionally intelligent, and strategic professional to serve as Strategic Business Operations Manager to the executive team. Working closely with Business Operations, Chief of Staff, CEO, and COO, this role will help drive clarity, accountability, and execution across the organization.&nbsp;

You'll serve as a force multiplier to executive leadership, helping advance the company's most important strategic initiatives, strengthen cross-functional coordination, and ensure priorities translate into action. You'll also help improve how the business operates and bring business performance to life through clear analysis, metrics, and compelling visual storytelling.&nbsp;

This is a high-impact, high-visibility role that requires exceptional judgment, attention to detail, and the ability to build trust across the organization. You'll begin by developing a deep understanding of Bishop Fox's business, operating model, and strategic priorities. As you build context and relationships, you'll take on increasing ownership of complex initiatives and become a trusted partner to executive leadership.&nbsp;

The ideal candidate is someone who can anticipate needs, navigate competing priorities, and bring structure to ambiguity while maintaining a collaborative, low-ego approach. You know how to get things done through others, communicate effectively at all levels, and ensure nothing falls through the cracks.&nbsp;

Responsibilities&nbsp;

Executive Enablement&nbsp;

• Partner with Business Operations and the Chief of Staff to advance CEO- and COO-sponsored strategic initiatives, translating executive priorities into coordinated action.&nbsp;

• Support executive prioritization and decision-making by synthesizing information, identifying trade-offs, and surfacing issues requiring leadership attention.&nbsp;

• Support the executive operating rhythm, including Board meetings, executive team meetings, all-hands, investor updates, and key external engagements.&nbsp;

• Develop and refine executive communications, presentations, Board materials, internal memos, and stakeholder updates.&nbsp;

• Ensure leadership decisions translate into clear actions, ownership, and follow-through.&nbsp;

Strategic Planning &amp; Execution&nbsp;

• Partner with Business Operations and executive leadership to plan, implement, and track strategic initiatives across the business.&nbsp;

• Support strategic planning, quarterly priorities, executive reviews, and leadership offsites.&nbsp;

• Translate strategic objectives into actionable plans with clear milestones, ownership, and measures of success.&nbsp;

• Coordinate cross-functional workstreams, proactively identifying dependencies, resolving blockers, and driving accountability.&nbsp;

